@@ -443,6 +443,14 @@ Local salvo delays never decrease in closest-silo slot order. A delayed or faile
 head queues its tail, and a queued retry prevents later bombs of that same salvo
 from overtaking it. Otherwise the engine can assign a different silo than the
 one used to price its trajectory and flight time.
+Each planned Atom retains whether its route is useful or intentional filler.
+Queued salvos retain the existing destination SAM capacity checks. Dispatch
+rechecks the actual source and current destination coverage after the worker
+probe and refreshes flight
+time, so a captured silo cannot redirect a useful Atom into unbudgeted cover.
+When that route has transit SAM coverage, the shared interceptor scheduler checks
+live slot reload times and native launch delay. Only a conclusive impossible
+interception clears the shot; missing or inconclusive forecasts remain blocked.
 SAM-salvo revalidation counts charges that can reload by the latest remaining
 planned arrival, including delayed-launch retries. Unknown flight or reload data
 keeps the conservative full-capacity estimate.
